# onnxruntime-node (pulled in by the optional @huggingface/transformers) downloads a
# multi-hundred-MB CUDA/GPU build on linux/x64 even when there is no GPU. If that download fails,
# npm drops the failed optional package AND @huggingface/transformers with it, then exits 0 — so
# the build dies later on TS2307 in a place that mentions neither CUDA nor a download.
#
# Measured on burst-i9 2026-08-12, same lockfile and host: without this line `npm ci` installs 207
# packages and loses transformers (`Error: socket hang up`); with it, 238 packages and the download
# is never attempted.
#
# CAVEAT: npm prints `Unknown project config "onnxruntime-node-install-cuda" — this will stop
# working in the next major version of npm`. It is honoured today (onnxruntime's script reads
# `npm_config_onnxruntime_node_install_cuda`), and the equivalent that will outlive it is the
# environment variable ONNXRUNTIME_NODE_INSTALL_CUDA=skip. Move to that when npm drops the config.
onnxruntime-node-install-cuda=skip
